Both deliverables are in: `impl/d1_race.c` (via the `impl -> impl_3` symlink) and the appended Round d1_r3 section in `strategies/d1_race.md`. The scoring node's own wisdom file showed r2's losses were two distinct diseases — a cold-cache wrong verdict at 4096 B=256, and correctly-picked arms running 15–32% slower in-process than standalone at 10007 B=64 / 16384-chain — fixed respectively by warm-per-sample racing (salts bumped to exe.r3/chn.r2) and a post-race replan of the winner on a clean heap; plus two sibling-requested variant lanes (`d1_composite -DUSE_ZMM2X2`, `d1_planner -DLANE_MAX_N=16384`). All tested cells pass check.py and the map-chain gate, repeatable across processes.

Technique: warm-verdict racing (warm_each) + clean-heap winner replan + sibling-requested variant lanes; best wallaby: 0.009 µs/xform at L=13 B=1 and 0.027 µs/xform at L=32 B=512 chained (4096 B=256 at 9.59, 100003 B=8 at 2347); rel L2 1.4e-16–1.1e-15, all under 1e-12.
